(a) Established. There is hereby created the position of Athens-Clarke County Marshal.
(b) Recognition and certification. The Athens-Clarke County Marshal shall do all things necessary in order to be recognized as a law enforcement officer of the state and certified within the standards of the Georgia Peace Officer Standards and Training Act (POST Act), as provided in O.C.G.A. § 35-8-1 et seq. In the event the Athens-Clarke County Marshal is not POST certified, then he shall have 12 months from his hiring date in which to become POST certified.
(c) Power of arrest. The Athens-Clarke County Marshal shall have the power of arrest in the enforcement of all ordinances of Athens-Clarke County, Georgia, and the laws of the state.
(d) Duties and responsibilities. The primary duties and responsibilities of the Athens-Clarke County Marshal shall be as follows:
(1) To enforce all ordinances enacted by the mayor and commission of Athens-Clarke County;
(2) To issue warnings, notices of ordinance violation, and citations for court appearances for the violation of ordinances;
(3) To investigate and collect evidence of these ordinance violations;
(4) To respond to complaints of alleged ordinance violations;
(5) To appear and testify in court;
(6) To do any follow-up work that may be necessary;
(7) To ensure proper collection of fines;
(8) To coordinate enforcement efforts with the building inspection office, planning department office, public works department and any other department or division of Athens-Clarke County as may be deemed necessary.
(e) Placement of position. All employees in the Athens-Clarke County Marshal's Service shall be under the supervision of the Manager.
(Ord. of 12-2-2003, § 1)

